<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/13/apple-home-collection-lineup-261013-1791902813432-49e02b44ba.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p2">Apple revealed today that <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/introducing-apple-home-collection-a-new-lineup-of-smart-home-accessories/" rel="noopener noreferrer">it has partnered with LG Electronics and Schneider Electric on the Apple Home Collection</a>, a range of smart home products including sensors, thermostats, cameras, and a smart lock that will be available beginning in December and into 2027.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/13/apple-home-collection-lifestyle-01-261013-1791902818424-7d8a3c50bf.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p4">LG has developed a video doorbell, a floodlight camera, outdoor and indoor cameras, a thermostat, and a temperature sensor, along with a smart lock that supports Ultra Wideband for hands-free door unlocking. Schneider Electric will offer a smart thermostat and temperature and humidity sensors. Device installation will also be available through a partnership between ADT and Apple Retail in the U.S. for an additional fee.</p>
<div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/13/apple-home-collection-schneider-home-smart-thermostat-261013-1791902823187-64827bc11f.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p6">Standout features include:</p>
<ul id="ul7"><li>the ability of the cameras to pick out faces, animals, vehicles, and packages,</li>
<li>iCloud+ support for HomeKit Secure Video,</li>
<li>the ability for the indoor cameras to tilt down when a household member returns home,</li>
<li>adaptive temperature on the thermostat that adjusts heating and cooling according to whether someone is home, and</li>
<li>the ability to shift heating and cooling use (U.S. only) to when available energy sources are cleaner.</li>
</ul><div class="media-wrapper"><img decoding="async" src="https://cdn.macstories.net/images/uploads/2026/10/13/apple-home-collection-lg-indoor-cam-plug-in-261013-1791902820912-5a0826fb00.jpg" alt="Source: Apple."><p class="image-caption">Source: Apple.</p></div>
<p id="p9">Pricing for the devices is as follows:</p>
<ul id="ul10"><li><strong>LG Video Doorbell Wired:</strong> $249.95</li>
<li><strong>LG Floodlight Cam:</strong> $399.95</li>
<li><strong>LG Outdoor Cam Plug-In:</strong> $299.95</li>
<li><strong>LG Indoor Cam Plug-In:</strong> $199.95</li>
<li><strong>LG Smart Deadbolt Lock:</strong> $349.95</li>
<li><strong>LG Smart Thermostat:</strong> $199.95</li>
<li><strong>LG Temperature Sensor:</strong> $39.95</li>
<li><strong>Schneider Home Smart Thermostat:</strong> $199.95</li>
<li><strong>Schneider Home Room Sensor:</strong> $39.95</li>
</ul><p id="p11">The cameras will be available in the U.S., Canada, and the UK, with other devices limited to the U.S. and Canada.</p>
